# Secrets and agents

Deploy and runtime secrets live in SOPS-encrypted `docker/envs/*/credentials.yaml`, `docker/envs/*/dc-backup-tls.yaml`, `docker/envs/*/dc-backup.yaml`, `.env.local`, and related env files. Those paths are in `.cursorignore`.

## Never run (or ask the user to run for you)

- `sops -d` on credential or `dc-backup*` files, or any command that prints decrypted YAML/JSON
- `gopass show` / `pass show` / reading from a secrets manager into the terminal
- `uv run dk <env> secrets` or `uv run dk <env> dc-backup …` when it would display or write secrets interactively in this session
- `cat`, `head`, `less`, or `Read` on decrypted credential content
- `docker compose config` (or `dk * config`) solely to inspect expanded secret env vars

## Safe checks

- Confirm encrypted files exist: `test -f docker/envs/staging/credentials.yaml`
- Verify SOPS can decrypt without printing values:

```bash
sops -d docker/envs/staging/credentials.yaml >/dev/null && echo "SOPS OK"
```

- Use `credentials.example.yaml` and `info.yaml` for structure (non-secret defaults only)

## If secrets are required

Ask the user to run decrypt/edit commands locally outside the agent, or to paste only non-sensitive outcomes (e.g. "SOPS OK", "deploy succeeded").
